<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/specifications/level6-evidence> {
  ex:l6-power-art a cd:MediaAsset ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level6-power.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Prospective two-sided known-SD Normal z-test power versus standardized true departure, with alpha 0.05 and independent sample sizes 5,10,20. Larger samples reach a given detection probability at smaller departures; all curves have null rejection probability 0.05. This known-SD illustration is not a t-test power calculation."@en ; dct:description "Example: known SD 0.5 µg/L and a true mean departure of 0.25 µg/L put us at 0.5 on the horizontal axis. Detection chance is about 20% with five independent measurements and 61% with twenty. Two-sided Normal z-test, alpha 5%; plotted points are joined by straight lines. These are not t-test power values."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-design-art a cd:MediaAsset ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level6-design.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Three sampling designs: fixed target, independent groups and matched units linked across two occasions. Connections mean real pairing, not a measured effect."@en ; dct:description "- Fixed reference: one estimated mean.\n- Separate upstream/downstream sites: independent-group comparison.\n- Same oxidation batch before/end: paired comparison."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-tail-art a cd:MediaAsset ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level6-tail-logic.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Upper-tail t example with ν = 9 at the null mean boundary. Shading to the right of observed t = 2 counts results at least this high under H₀. The probability includes the tail beyond the drawing."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-cliff-art a cd:MediaAsset ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level6-cliff-grid.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "For X values 1,2,2 and Y values 2,3,4 a.u., a three-by-three labelled pair grid contains zero X wins, seven losses and two ties. Both ties occur against Y equal to 2. Repeated X equal to 2 remains two observations."@en ; dct:description "- X wins 0, loses 7 and ties 2 of nine comparisons.\n- Half credit for ties gives U for X equal to 1.\n- Six original observations, not nine independent units."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-design-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "One target, separate groups, or paired batches?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-rank-grid-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Nine comparisons: who wins, loses or ties?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
}

